# Databricks notebook source
# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC # Table & Column Usage Scanner
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Walks every notebook and code file under the configured workspace folders, parses the
# MAGIC SQL (`%sql` cells, `spark.sql(...)` strings, `.sql` files) and the PySpark DataFrame code
# MAGIC (`spark.table`, `spark.read.table`, `select`, `withColumn`, `F.col`, `join`, `saveAsTable`, ...)
# MAGIC and writes **one row per script / schema / table / column** used.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC **How to use:** import this file into your workspace, attach it to a cluster, set the widgets at the
# MAGIC top, then *Run all*. The result is written to the CSV path (and, optionally, a Delta table) and displayed.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Output columns: `script_path, script_type, language, cell_no, source_kind, access_type,
# MAGIC catalog_name, schema_name, table_name, column_name, resolution`
# MAGIC
# MAGIC `resolution` tells you how sure the mapping is:
# MAGIC | value | meaning |
# MAGIC |---|---|
# MAGIC | `VERIFIED` | column confirmed to exist in that table (via information_schema) |
# MAGIC | `QUALIFIED` | SQL column explicitly tied to the table (`t.col` or single-table query) |
# MAGIC | `SINGLE_SOURCE` | DataFrame column on a DataFrame built from exactly one table |
# MAGIC | `VIA_STAR` / `VIA_TEMP_VIEW` / `VIA_UNION` | traced through `SELECT *`, a temp view, or a DataFrame union |
# MAGIC | `INFERRED` | column was ambiguous, but every other candidate table was ruled out |
# MAGIC | `STAR` / `STAR_EXPANDED` | `SELECT *` (expanded to real columns when the schema is known) |
# MAGIC | `AMBIGUOUS` | column could belong to any of several joined tables (one row per candidate) |
# MAGIC | `TABLE_ONLY` | table used but no specific column could be identified (e.g. `count(*)`, writes) |
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Can also run outside Databricks on an exported folder:
# MAGIC `python table_column_usage_scanner.py --path ./my_export --out usage.csv [--schema-csv cols.csv]`

